file=Shared OS/skills/ponytail-help/SKILL.md · h=name: ponytail-help\ndescription: >\nQuick-reference card for all ponytail modes, skills, and commands.\nOne-shot display, not a persistent mode. Trigger: /ponytail-help,\n"ponytail help", "what ponytail commands", "how do I use ponytail".\n · ph:Ponytail Help=Display this reference card when invoked. One-shot, do NOT change mode,\nwrite flag files, or persist anything.\n · tb=\| Level \| Trigger \| What change \| · tb=\|-------\|---------\|-------------\| · tb=\| **Lite** \| `/ponytail lite` \| Build what's asked, name the lazier alternative in one line. \| · tb=\| **Full** \| `/ponytail` \| The ladder enforced: YAGNI → stdlib → native → one line → minimum. Default. \| · tb=\| **Ultra** \| `/ponytail ultra` \| YAGNI extremist. Deletion before addition. Challenges requirements before building. \| · l:Levels=Level sticks until changed or session end.\n · tb=\| Skill \| Trigger \| What it does \| · tb=\|-------\|---------\|--------------\| · tb=\| **ponytail** \| `/ponytail` \| Lazy mode itself. Simplest solution that works. \| · tb=\| **ponytail-review** \| `/ponytail-review` \| Over-engineering review: `L42: yagni: factory, one product. Inline.` \| · tb=\| **ponytail-gain** \| `/ponytail-gain` \| Measured-impact scoreboard: less code, less cost, more speed. \| · tb=\| **ponytail-help** \| `/ponytail-help` \| This card. \| · s:Skills=Codex uses `@ponytail`, `@ponytail-review`, and `@ponytail-help`; Claude Code\nand OpenCode use the slash-command forms above (OpenCode ships `/ponytail` and\n`/ponytail-review`).\n · d:Deactivate=Say "stop ponytail" or "normal mode". Resume anytime with `/ponytail`.\n`/ponytail off` also works.\n · cdm:Configure Default Mode=Default mode = `full`, auto-active every session. Change it:\n\n**Environment variable** (highest priority):\n```bash\nexport PONYTAIL_DEFAULT_MODE=ultra\n```\n\n**Config file** (`~/.config/ponytail/config.json`, Windows: `%APPDATA%\ponytail\config.json`):\n```json\n{ "defaultMode": "lite" }\n```\n\nSet `"off"` to disable auto-activation on session start, activate manually\nwith `/ponytail` when wanted.\n\nResolution: env var > config file > `full`.\n · u:Update=Enable auto-update once: open `/plugin`, go to Marketplaces, pick ponytail, Enable auto-update. Claude Code then pulls new versions at startup (run `/reload-plugins` when it prompts). Manual refresh: `/plugin marketplace update ponytail` then `/reload-plugins`.\n\nIf `/plugin` is not recognized, your Claude Code is out of date. Update it (`npm install -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code@latest`, or `brew upgrade claude-code`) and restart. Other hosts use their own update flow.\n · m:More=Full docs + examples: https://github.com/DietrichGebert/ponytail\n